{
  "_comment": [
    "Canned Authentik API responses for scripts/smoke.ts, driven through the",
    "injectable HTTP layer so the smoke test needs no network and no Authentik.",
    "",
    "Each list endpoint holds an array of *pages*; the stub in smoke.ts wraps page N",
    "in the appropriate envelope. `core/applications` has two pages on purpose, and",
    "`outposts/instances` is wrapped in the DRF-style envelope while the others use",
    "Authentik's own `{pagination:{next}}` shape — both are read, so both are tested.",
    "",
    "Field names and shapes follow Authentik's REST API: providers are referenced from",
    "an application by pk and embedded as `provider_obj` / `backchannel_providers_obj`,",
    "a proxy provider's `internal_host` lives on the provider endpoint rather than on",
    "the application, and `redirect_uris` appears in both the object-list and the",
    "newline-delimited-string form that different versions return.",
    "",
    "`mode` on a proxy provider changes what `external_host` means: in forward_single",
    "and proxy mode it is the application's own hostname, but in forward_domain mode it",
    "is the authentication domain shared by every application in that domain — pk 12 is",
    "here to prove that one is not matched on.",
    "",
    "The OIDC applications on page 2 each exercise exactly one matching rule and are",
    "unreachable by the others, so a reverted rule leaves a service unmatched rather",
    "than merely matched for a different reason: `nb-app` only by the container name",
    "inside a redirect URI, `ha-portal` only by the application name once separators",
    "are normalized, `fin-01` only by its provider name once the mechanism words are",
    "dropped. `s01` (provider \"DB Provider\", a two-character residue) and `ext-01` (a",
    "redirect URI on an IP literal, whose port the identity provider publishes) must",
    "match nothing, and pk 22 gives the ambiguous `pair` application a provider so a",
    "match arbitrated between its two services would visibly claim a gate.",
    "",
    "`core/applications:withheld` is not an endpoint. It holds the applications the real",
    "`/core/applications/` would refuse to return: that view drops `meta_hide`, paginates,",
    "and only then filters the page through the policy engine as the token's own user, so",
    "a least-privilege token is served a subset. The stub models both sides of that — it",
    "serves `core/applications` alone by default and appends this key as a further page",
    "when `superuser_full_list=true` is honoured, while reporting `count` as the sum in",
    "*both* modes, which is what makes the shortfall detectable at all.",
    "",
    "The three withheld applications take the three possible outcomes. `rec-01` is",
    "assigned oauth2 provider pk 28, which the provider endpoints do return (they are",
    "permission-filtered, not policy-filtered, and every provider names its application),",
    "so it is rebuilt and its redirect URI ties it to the `archive` stack by container",
    "address. `wh-02` is rebuilt the same way but its provider addresses an unrelated",
    "external host, so it is recovered and then goes unmatched — the case that proves a",
    "rebuilt record is reported as the narrower thing it is. `hidden-01` is assigned a",
    "SAML provider, a kind LabView does not read, so nothing names it and it stays",
    "unaccounted for — the case recovery cannot close, and the only one that keeps the",
    "partial phase from being an artefact of an incomplete fixture. Every provider",
    "here carries `assigned_application_*`, so the recovery pass also has to prefer the",
    "listed record for the eleven it would otherwise duplicate. No provider is assigned",
    "through the backchannel pair; those fields are present and null throughout."
  ],

